userStories.description:
**Goal** — Preserve the commit SHA produced by each finish fix round in the live audit trail and terminal result.

**Motivation** — `commitFixes()` returns `shaAfter`; the flow destructures it, uses it only for the gate route, and drops it, so "Fixed in `<sha>`" can only be reconstructed by matching round timestamps against `git log`.

**Approach** — Extend `FinishRound` with an optional SHA and pass `shaAfter` into the existing `appendRound` payload only when the round committed. Keep the append-only JSONL contract and its best-effort failure behavior unchanged; `readRounds` and `writeResult` must continue to pass serialized round objects through unchanged.

**Scope** — In: `FinishRound`, the `commit_<phase>` payload, and existing round/result tests. Out: PR body rendering and artifact loading belong to US-002 through US-004; forge writes belong to US-005.

**Interface**
```typescript
export interface FinishRound {
  ts: string;
  phase: FinishPhase;
  attempt: number;
  committed: boolean;
  sha?: string;
  findings: Finding[];
  failing?: string[];
}
```

**Goal** — Add a pure flow-local builder that deterministically renders the finish PR title and markdown body from a supplied context.

**Motivation** — The finish flow currently opens with a hardcoded placeholder title and a one-sentence body, discarding every artifact the run just produced.

**Approach** — The body is assembled by **deterministic string joins over on-disk artifacts** — no model call, no LLM-written narrative. Every section is reproducible from files that exist before `open_pr` runs. Mirror `escapeTableCell` in `src/plugins/builtin/auto-pr/pr-body.ts:77`; a `|` in a story title otherwise breaks the column boundary. Title — `feat: <feature>`, identical to `buildTitle` in `src/plugins/builtin/auto-pr/pr-body.ts:44`, so finish-opened and auto-PR-opened PRs read the same. The rendered PR body uses `##`-level section headings. A section whose source is empty renders **no heading at all**.

**Scope** — In: pure types, title/body formatting, escaped story rows, optional section omission, review headings/findings, and summary footer. Out: reading artifacts is US-003/US-004; wiring the builder into `open_pr` is US-005; do not share code with `src/` or change auto-PR behavior.

**Interface**
```typescript
export interface FinishPrStory {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  acCount: number;
}

export interface FinishPrContext {
  feature: string;
  stories: FinishPrStory[];
  outOfScope: string[];
  acceptance?: string;
  regression?: string;
  gatesRan: string[];
  diffstat?: string;
  rounds: FinishRound[];
  run: {
    durationMs?: number;
    storiesPassed?: number;
    storiesTotal?: number;
  };
}

/** Pure. No I/O. */
export function buildFinishTitle(ctx: FinishPrContext): string;
export function buildFinishBody(ctx: FinishPrContext): string;
```

**Goal** — Extend the finish PR context loader to read PRD stories/out-of-scope data and sibling status outcomes without blocking a finish run.

**Motivation** — Every fact in the replacement body comes from artifacts nax has already written, but PRD and status fields are not currently assembled for `open_pr`.

**Approach** — `loadFinishPrContext` is I/O and reads the artifacts below; never throws. Read `userStories[]` as id/title/acceptanceCriteria length and `outOfScope[]` from `input.prdPath`; read `postRun.acceptance.status`, `postRun.regression.status`, `durationMs`, and `progress.passed`/`progress.total` from sibling `status.json`. Resolve the sibling path against `input.workdir` when `prdPath` is relative. Missing, unreadable, or unparseable PRD yields empty stories/out-of-scope; missing, unreadable, or unparseable status leaves optional values undefined.

**Scope** — In: Node read dependency injection and fail-open PRD/status parsing. Out: rounds/diffstat/gates are US-004; body formatting is US-002; forge invocation is US-005; do not add fields to either artifact schema.

**Interface**
```typescript
/** I/O. Reads the artifacts below; never throws. */
export function loadFinishPrContext(
  input: FinishInput,
  args: { base: string; gatesRan: string[] },
): Promise<FinishPrContext>;
```

**Goal** — Complete the finish PR context with audit rounds, green gate names, and the branch diffstat.

**Motivation** — The auto-created draft is composed before finish completes and therefore carries no acceptance result, gate result, or review findings.

**Approach** — Pass `readRounds(input)` through to `FinishPrContext.rounds`, take `gatesRan` from the caller, and invoke `git diff --stat <base>...HEAD` through injectable `_prBodyDeps.run`. Its stdout becomes `diffstat` only on success; a non-zero diff must leave it undefined without throwing. Widen `gateOutputs` from `{ failing?: string[] }` to include `ran?: string[]` so the green `quality_gates` output is readable at `open_pr`. Keep all Node-only I/O and fail-open behavior in the flow-local builder.

**Scope** — In: loader completion, diff command invocation, and `gateOutputs.ran` exposure. Out: title/body presentation is US-002; PRD/status parsing is US-003; flow and forge writes are US-005.

**Interface**
```typescript
export function gateOutputs(ctx: OutputsCtx): { failing?: string[]; ran?: string[] };

export function loadFinishPrContext(
  input: FinishInput,
  args: { base: string; gatesRan: string[] },
): Promise<FinishPrContext>;
```
